### 🟡 MEDIUM

#### 5. Eager Test
**File:** `OrderProcessorTests.cs` · **Method:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 52)
```csharp
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
Assert.AreEqual("Completed", order.Status);
```
**Problem:** 7 distinct production methods called. A failure could come from any of them, making diagnosis painful.
**Fix:** If this is intended as an integration test, mark it with `[TestCategory("Integration")]` to set expectations. Otherwise, break it into focused unit tests (one per method) and test the workflow via a single high-level orchestration method.

