## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix effort | Why first |
|----------|-------|-----------|-----------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~5 min | Tests that verify *nothing* are actively dangerous — false confidence |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~10 min | Hidden untested branch right now |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~5 min | Flake risk + 2 s wasted per run |
| 4 | Mystery Guest | ~5 min | Fails on every machine without that file |
| 5 | Exception Handling | ~2 min | One-line swap to `Assert.ThrowsException` |
| 6 | Magic Number + Assertion Roulette | ~10 min | Same method, fix together |
| 7 | Sensitive Equality | ~5 min | Fragile to formatting changes |
| 8 | Eager Test | ~15 min | Split or annotate as integration |
| 9 | General Fixture | ~1 min | Delete one unused field |

All 10 findings map to the **testsmells.org** academic taxonomy (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020). Smells 1–10 in the core catalog plus **Assertion Roulette** from the extended catalog.
